From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] z-offset: zMod's storage only where zMod's _TEST_POINT exists

Kiln OS's zmod-compat plugin (on by default) defines SAVE_ZMOD_DATA so
that zMod-made G-code runs, and SAVE_ZMOD_DATA alone selected the ZMOD
row. Kiln keeps the Z offset as save_variables zoffset through its
SET_GCODE_OFFSET wrapper (the Helper-Script layout) and has no
_TEST_POINT macro, so every idle save first sent SET_GCODE_VARIABLE
MACRO=_TEST_POINT, Klipper refused it, and the offset was not saved
(djvalic/kiln-os#57). The ZMOD row now also needs _TEST_POINT, which
zMod's own SET_GCODE_OFFSET reads; without it, Kiln resolves to the
Helper-Script row.

Tests: SAVE_ZMOD_DATA alone is no provider; SAVE_ZMOD_DATA with the
SET_GCODE_OFFSET wrapper is Helper-Script, sends no _TEST_POINT clear
or LOAD_ZOFFSET, and reads zoffset back. The zMod test printers carry
_TEST_POINT.
---
 src/printer/z_offset_persistence.cpp          | 15 ++++-
 .../test_moonraker_subscription_fields.cpp    |  2 +
 tests/unit/test_print_tune_zoffset_adjust.cpp |  2 +-
 .../unit/test_printer_state_capabilities.cpp  |  2 +-
 tests/unit/test_z_offset_adjust.cpp           |  4 +-
 tests/unit/test_z_offset_calibration_send.cpp |  2 +-
 tests/unit/test_z_offset_persistence.cpp      | 66 +++++++++++++++----
 7 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/printer/z_offset_persistence.cpp b/src/printer/z_offset_persistence.cpp
index fda7c6ef..5d6460d7 100644
--- a/src/printer/z_offset_persistence.cpp
+++ b/src/printer/z_offset_persistence.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@ struct Provider {
     const char* name;
     /// Macro whose presence identifies the firmware.
     const char* detect_macro;
+    /// A second macro the firmware always has, or nullptr. Needed where the
+    /// detect macro can be defined by something else for compatibility.
+    const char* confirm_macro;
     /// Status objects that carry the stored value.
     std::vector<std::string> status_objects;
     /// One-shot command that turns persistence on, or nullptr.
@@ -230,6 +233,13 @@ const std::vector<Provider>& providers() {
     static const std::vector<Provider> table = {
         {"ZMOD",
          "SAVE_ZMOD_DATA",
+         // Kiln OS: its zmod-compat plugin defines SAVE_ZMOD_DATA so that
+         // zMod-made G-code runs, but it keeps the offset as the
+         // Helper-Script row's `zoffset`, and it has no _TEST_POINT, whose
+         // variable this row clears before every idle adjustment (the
+         // command fails there and the save with it). zMod's own
+         // SET_GCODE_OFFSET reads _TEST_POINT, so zMod always has it.
+         "_TEST_POINT",
          {"save_variables"},
          "SAVE_ZMOD_DATA LOAD_ZOFFSET=1",
          "SET_GCODE_VARIABLE MACRO=_TEST_POINT VARIABLE=temp_z_offset VALUE=0",
@@ -245,6 +255,7 @@ const std::vector<Provider>& providers() {
          &toolchanger_addon::zmod_c5_present},
         {"Forge-X",
          "SET_MOD",
+         nullptr,
          {"mod_params"},
          "SET_MOD PARAM=\"load_zoffset\" VALUE=1",
          nullptr,
@@ -268,6 +279,7 @@ const std::vector<Provider>& providers() {
         // refuted_helper_script().
         {"Helper-Script",
          "SET_GCODE_OFFSET",
+         nullptr,
          {"save_variables"},
          nullptr,
          nullptr,
@@ -283,7 +295,8 @@ const std::vector<Provider>& providers() {
 
 const Provider* match(const PrinterDiscovery& hw) {
     for (const auto& p : providers()) {
-        if (hw.has_macro(p.detect_macro)) {
+        if (hw.has_macro(p.detect_macro) &&
+            (!p.confirm_macro || hw.has_macro(p.confirm_macro))) {
             return &p;
         }
     }
